      <li><strong>SP20</strong>: 20% off all plans, tested and confirmed working at checkout on the web store</li>
      <li><strong>TRAVELESIMEXPERT</strong>: 20% off, also tested and confirmed working, despite Instabridge's own description flagging it as a new-user coupon</li>
      <li><strong>DPF10</strong>: no longer works. We tested it at checkout and it came back invalid, so we've pulled it from the top spot.</li>
    </ul>
    <p style="margin-top:.75rem;margin-bottom:0;color:#63553F;">Both working codes give the same 20%, so either is fine. Enter the code on Instabridge's web store, not in the phone app, see below for why that matters.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Real operational note instead of generic feature grid / comparison table -->
  <h2>Free WiFi First, eSIM as Backup, Not the Other Way Around</h2>
  <p>
    If you're comparing Instabridge to a pure eSIM app on price alone, you're missing the actual pitch. The app itself is free to install and use for hotspot access, no purchase required, and the eSIM only gets bought when you decide the free WiFi isn't cutting it. That makes the eSIM pricing here closer to a top-up than a primary purchase decision: check the free hotspot map for your destination first, then buy a data plan only for the gaps.
  </p>
  <p>
    That also means Instabridge's eSIM plans are data-only, no calls or texts, and a plan doesn't roll over or top up automatically once it runs out. Buy based on what you actually expect to use past whatever free WiFi you can find, not on a flat "just get the biggest plan" instinct.
  </p>

  <!-- Owner-confirmed operational note -->
  <h2>Promo Codes Only Work on the Web Store, Not in the App</h2>
  <p>
    This trips people up: you cannot enter a promo or discount code inside the Instabridge phone app. We confirmed this directly with Instabridge's own support chat, which told us plainly that a travel eSIM promo code has to be entered at <strong>store.instabridge.com/mobile-data</strong> during checkout, and that promo codes "can't be entered directly in the app."
  </p>
  <p>
    Instabridge's app does have its own separate "Redeem eSIM Coupon Code" option (under Menu/More in the app), but that's a different system for a different kind of code, not a stand-in for the checkout promo codes on this page. If you're in the app looking for a place to type SP20 or TRAVELESIMEXPERT and can't find one, that's why: buy through the web store link above instead.
  </p>

