  <!-- Decision help -->
  <h2>Is Instabridge the Right Pick for Your Trip</h2>
  <div class="decision-grid">
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--good">
      <h3>Good fit</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You're headed somewhere with decent hotspot density (major cities, tourist-heavy regions) and mostly want a free-WiFi-first backup plan</li>
        <li>You want one app for both hotspot hunting and a data top-up, instead of juggling two</li>
        <li>Your data needs are light enough that an eSIM is a backup, not your main connection</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--alt">
      <h3>Consider alternatives</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You want the lowest possible per-GB price for a data-heavy trip: <a href="/airhub/">Airhub</a> runs cheaper per gigabyte on most destinations</li>
        <li>You're headed somewhere rural or off the beaten path where a hotspot-sharing database is unlikely to have much coverage: a straight per-GB eSIM like <a href="/redteago/">RedteaGO</a> doesn't depend on other travelers having been there first</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

