  <!-- FAQ -->
  <h2>Instabridge Promo Code FAQ</h2>
  <div class="content-faq">
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>What is the best code right now</h3>
      <p><strong>SP20</strong> or <strong>TRAVELESIMEXPERT</strong>: both 20% off, and both personally tested and confirmed working at checkout on the web store. DPF10, previously listed here, no longer works and has been dropped.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Why can't I find a promo code field in the Instabridge app</h3>
      <p>Because there isn't one. Instabridge's own support confirmed that promo and discount codes only work at checkout on the web store (store.instabridge.com/mobile-data), not typed directly into the phone app. The app has a separate "Redeem eSIM Coupon Code" option, but that's a different feature, not a substitute.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Is the free WiFi actually free</h3>
      <p>Yes. Instabridge's core product is a database of over 20 million community-submitted WiFi hotspot passwords, free to use in the app with no purchase required. The eSIM is a separate paid product for when free WiFi isn't available or fast enough.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Does Instabridge include calls or texts</h3>
      <p>No. Instabridge eSIM plans are data-only.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Can I get a refund on an Instabridge eSIM</h3>
      <p>We haven't confirmed a clear refund policy for eSIM purchases, so don't count on one. Check Instabridge's own terms before you buy if that matters to your trip.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>How many countries does Instabridge cover</h3>
      <p>Instabridge advertises eSIM coverage in 190+ countries, plus its separate free WiFi hotspot database which is strongest in well-travelled cities.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

